# Real APISIX → Redirect connection-stage review

Conclusion: the current119-error cluster is specifically APISIX upstream connection establishment, concentrated in container worker50. It is not evidence of a slow302 handler or Kafka-consumer throughput failure. Worker-local scheduling/event processing delay is the leading candidate; keepalive retirement could be a trigger, but neither has a causal trace yet. Do not increase timeout, backlog or keepalive request count based on this review.

No product, runtime settings, JAR, profile evidence or resource was changed. The source lane is stopped; future fine-grained diagnostics require a separate bounded implementation and acceptance.

## Confirmed installed path

The six local source copies come from the bound currently running APISIX CID `d12e311ccb6159b2df9f110601a2062e623f221951457e1257d6e7ade4d4de0e`, image `sha256:178d1f79c2c39834f50213bf6ace90284f6b985dc8189cc50f3666d9fb1037ad`, init/master PID29899. Before/after identity assertions completed. Collection limitations are recorded below.

| Exact source site | Fact and consequence |
|---|---|
| [rendered nginx.conf:140](../../../../../.work/real-fanout-20260909/upstream-review-source-usr_local_apisix_conf_nginx.conf:140) | `apisix_backend` has `keepalive320`, `keepalive_requests1000`, `keepalive_timeout60s` at143–145. These are upstream settings, distinct from client-side keepalive. |
| [installed balancer.lua:287](../../../../../.work/real-fanout-20260909/upstream-review-source-usr_local_apisix_apisix_balancer.lua:287) | Reads explicit `upstream_conf.keepalive_pool`, otherwise cached `nginx_config.http.upstream` defaults. At316 the pool key is scheme + host + port;328 selects peer with pool size,334 calls `enable_keepalive(idle_timeout,requests)`. The HTTP redirect peer therefore uses `http#172.17.0.1#8003`, not a separate pool per short code, user or source IP. |
| [schema_def.lua:414](../../../../../.work/real-fanout-20260909/upstream-review-source-usr_local_apisix_apisix_schema_def.lua:414) | Explicit pool object defaults also size320, idle_timeout60, requests1000. Changing size or request lifetime is a different variable from raising an application queue limit. |
| [installed ngx.balancer:220](../../../../../.work/real-fanout-20260909/upstream-review-source-usr_local_openresty_lualib_ngx_balancer.lua:220) | Validates idle timeout/max requests and passes both to the HTTP FFI at251–252. This verifies the installed Lua/API mapping; the C retirement branch was not captured, and no connection was observed reaching its1000th request. |
